  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nFutures are painting red across the board with tech leading the selloff - QQQ down 3.22% while SPY holds relatively better at -1.70%. VIX spiking to 24.89 signals real fear ahead of NFP, and the geopolitical headlines from Iran aren't helping risk sentiment.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>NFP Release (8:30 AM EST)</strong> - The big kahuna. All employment metrics dropping at once with high impact ratings</li>\n<li><strong>Iran Escalation</strong> - Multiple headlines about missile warnings at US warships and new sanctions creating oil volatility</li>\n<li><strong>Boeing Production News</strong> - 737 Max assembly line restart July 6th could move industrials</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Earnings Aftermath</strong> - XLK down over 5% suggests lingering concerns from this week's reports</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Tech's -5.11% pre-market drop combined with Iran tensions creates perfect storm for broader market breakdown below key support levels.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClassic risk-off rotation in play with defensive sectors leading - Consumer Staples up 2.01%, Healthcare +1.72%, and Utilities +1.12%. Tech's massive 5.11% gap down is dragging growth while safe havens catch bids. Energy surprisingly weak at -1.48% despite Middle East tensions.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>NFP at 8:30 AM will either rescue this selloff or accelerate it. With VIX above 24, expect violent moves in either direction.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 740</strong> - Key support from May lows; break here opens door to 720s</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 710</strong> - Major technical level; already testing in pre-market</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 27</strong> - Next resistance that would signal full panic mode</li>\n<li><strong>XLK 180</strong> - Tech sector ETF critical support that's getting tested hard</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Strong NFP could reverse this morning's weakness quickly, especially if wage growth disappoints and eases Fed concerns.</div>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
